
Round 2 "FIGHT"
Lets store that data. 

So Junos already had a big easy button for archival file transfer :) via syslog..

But wait theres more..  I also figured out you can log / save to a usbkey :) .  I have done this in places backups over the network were not an option. :/ 
**Make sure you format that slice as vfat so PC can play too..
start shell user root
mount  /dev/da0s1 /mnt/   ** or whatever your usbslice is. 
{master:0}[edit system archival]
spiderman@ex4400-mp# show 
configuration {
    transfer-on-commit;
    archive-sites {
       file:///mnt/;
    }
}

But for those of us that need a more uniformed, scaled , and longer term way of dealing with this .. 
SYSLOG is the go to for me on this 
{master:0}[edit system syslog file tom-mac-learning.log]
spiderman@ex4400-mp# show 
archive {
    size 200m;
    files 3;
    world-readable;
    transfer-interval 1440;
    start-time "2026-11-15.04:30:00 -0500";
    archive-sites {
        "scp://jun0s-backup@parker.tom:/home/jun0s-backup/Juniper-mac-learning-logs/" password "$8$aes25"; ## SECRET-DATA
    }
}
